WEBVTT

1
00:00:19.790 --> 00:00:21.376
WOMAN:
<i>For thousands of years,</i>

2
00:00:21.459 --> 00:00:23.338
<i>they've been by our sides.</i>

3
00:00:25.760 --> 00:00:27.764
<i>Protecting us...</i>

4
00:00:29.810 --> 00:00:32.231
<i>...and comforting us.</i>

5
00:00:35.237 --> 00:00:37.701
<i>Pets make our world
a better place.</i>

6
00:00:40.707 --> 00:00:43.336
<i>That's why we want to make
the world better for them.</i>

7
00:00:45.090 --> 00:00:47.094
<i>We're Mars Petcare.</i>

8
00:01:29.387 --> 00:01:32.184
NARRATOR: <i>Who doesn't dream
of having superpowers?</i>

9
00:01:35.608 --> 00:01:37.654
<i>But what if I told you</i>

10
00:01:37.737 --> 00:01:41.578
<i>there are real superheroes
living among us?</i>

11
00:01:49.218 --> 00:01:52.266
<i>They could even be...
your best friend.</i>

12
00:01:55.940 --> 00:01:57.944
(WIND WHISTLING)

13
00:02:01.785 --> 00:02:03.789
(MAN PANTING)

14
00:02:20.656 --> 00:02:22.660
(RUMBLING)

15
00:02:40.738 --> 00:02:43.284
NARRATOR: <i>And that...
is where I come in.</i>

16
00:02:43.451 --> 00:02:45.455
(HELICOPTER APPROACHING)

17
00:02:50.758 --> 00:02:52.762
(INDISTINCT RADIO TRANSMISSION)

18
00:03:10.130 --> 00:03:12.467
MAN: <i>And we're approaching
the target, Ian.</i>

19
00:03:12.635 --> 00:03:13.929
<i>We've got an...</i>

20
00:03:14.096 --> 00:03:16.518
<i>avalanche pile
and a debris pile.</i>

21
00:03:16.852 --> 00:03:19.733
<i>We're going to put you down
on top of the debris.</i>

22
00:03:25.243 --> 00:03:27.122
<i>It's ten meters.</i>

23
00:03:28.374 --> 00:03:29.502
<i>Five...</i>

24
00:03:29.586 --> 00:03:31.715
<i>four... three...</i>

25
00:03:31.798 --> 00:03:33.636
<i>two... one.</i>

26
00:03:33.719 --> 00:03:35.347
<i>On the ground.</i>

27
00:03:37.267 --> 00:03:38.394
<i>Clear the line.</i>

28
00:03:56.430 --> 00:03:58.101
NARRATOR:
<i>They call me Henry.</i>

29
00:03:58.267 --> 00:04:00.271
<i>Whistler Mountain Ski Patrol.</i>

30
00:04:02.484 --> 00:04:05.156
<i>Along with
my two‐legged partner, Ian,</i>

31
00:04:05.323 --> 00:04:07.494
<i>we're your best hope
in an avalanche.</i>

32
00:04:28.537 --> 00:04:30.583
<i>It would take
a team of people</i>

33
00:04:30.666 --> 00:04:33.254
<i>hours to find you.</i>

34
00:04:33.421 --> 00:04:35.968
<i>I can do it in minutes.</i>

35
00:04:36.135 --> 00:04:38.139
(SNIFFING)

36
00:04:44.819 --> 00:04:46.155
(BARKING)

37
00:04:46.238 --> 00:04:48.076
‐IAN: What do you got?
‐(HENRY WHINES)

38
00:04:48.159 --> 00:04:50.121
That's a good dog.
Get him out of there.

39
00:04:50.205 --> 00:04:51.917
That's it,
get him out of there.

40
00:04:52.000 --> 00:04:54.088
‐That's a good dog. Yes!
‐(HENRY SNUFFLING)

41
